{
    "background_story": "Arlet was a brilliant and ambitious software engineer, known for her exceptional problem-solving skills. She thrived in the fast-paced tech industry, taking on increasingly complex projects and consistently delivering high-quality results. However, her tendency to overcommit soon led to an overload of responsibilities. Arlet found herself juggling multiple high-priority tasks, working late nights and weekends, and sacrificing her personal life. As the pressure mounted, she began to feel burnt out, struggling to keep up with the demands of her job. One day, her computer crashed, symbolizing the overload she felt. Arlet realized she needed to set boundaries and prioritize her well-being. She learned to say 'no' to non-essential tasks and focus on what truly mattered, finding a healthier balance between her work and personal life.",
